P4
  Change: AsyncStream::connect refuses a ServerAddress::Unix with
          ErrorKind::ProxyConnect when a SOCKS5 proxy is set, before any
          local dial. The message leaves the path out. A socket the user
          names never gets here under a proxy: the workspace refuses a
          socket uri with an ssh table and Client::with_options refuses a
          non-TCP seed with a proxy. P4 is defence in depth at dial time
          for any Unix address that would still reach the stream under a
          proxy. Without a proxy, P5 keeps an advertised socket from being
          dialled.
  Files: src/runtime/stream.rs
  Upstream: none filed (project rule: own issue and local workaround)

P5
  Change: TopologyDescription::initialize records the socket paths among
          the seeds in seed_sockets, and add_new_servers, the one place
          members a server advertises enter the topology, drops any
          ServerAddress::Unix not in that set, with or without a proxy.
          The driver turns any `*.sock` member a server reports into a
          Unix address, so a server could otherwise make this machine dial
          a local socket the connection never named; only seeds the uri
          names are dialled. A dropped member sets refused_socket, which
          adds a fixed, path-free "Refused:" note to the topology's
          Display, so the selection-timeout error says why. Known gap: the
          driver lowercases advertised host names but not seeds, so a seed
          path with upper-case letters never matches its advertised twin
          and is dropped; such a set fails closed (no primary). On non-unix
          builds Unix addresses do not exist, so the filter is unix-only.
  Files: src/sdam/description/topology.rs,
         src/sdam/description/topology/server_selection.rs,
         src/sdam/description/topology/server_selection/test.rs
  Upstream: none filed (project rule: own issue and local workaround)
